 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "users is a list of user names; randomInts supplies the random choices so that the result is reproducible (it has exactly 2 * floor(n / 2) entries, each in [0, 1e9]). Keep a pool equal to a copy of users. Repeatedly, while the pool has at least 2 users: take the next random value r, pick index r mod (pool size), remove that user by moving the last pool user into its slot; do the same with the next random value for the second user; record [first, second]. If one user remains, append [thatUser]. Return the list of pairs (and the final single).",
  "provenance": [
